9:42:16 AM [express] GET /api/content 200 in 8ms :: [{"id":2,"userId":3,"board":"CBSE","className":"Grade 1","subject":"English","chapter":"The animal song","topic":"","extractedText":"[Page 1]\n8. The _______________ _______________ is teaching English.  \n\n9. Squirrels love to eat _______________ _______________.  \n\n10. The _______________ _______________ is a cunning animal.  \n\n---\n\n**KNOW**  \n\n**PROPER NOUNS**  \nThe words **Simba**, **Bimbi**, **Luna**, **Bunny**, **Ray**, **Dale** and **Lee** have been specially given to the lion, lamb, rabbit and horse respectively. These words are called **special names** or **proper nouns**. They begin with a **capital letter**.  \n\n---\n\n**LEARN**  \n\nA. Write the answers.  \n1. Your name: ________________________  \n\n2. Your best friend: ________________________\n\n---\n\n[Page 2]\n### LEARN  \n#### A. Fill in the blanks with naming words from the box.\n\nBooks | Teacher | Car | Nuts | Grandfather  \n---|---|---|---|---  \nBicycle | Tiger | Hat | Fox | Ball  \n\n1. My _________ ran out of petrol.  \n2. A _________ is chasing a deer.  \n3. I love reading _________.  \n4. Cricket is played with a bat and a _________.  \n5. The red _________ looks beautiful on her head.  \n6. I ride a _________ every evening.  \n7. My _________ is 70 years old.\n\n---\n\n[Page 3]\nThe highlighted words in the sentences are **naming words**. Names of **people**, **places**, **animals** and **things** are called naming words.  \nNaming words are also called **nouns**.  \n\n---\n\n### **LEARN**  \n\n#### A. Match the pictures with the naming words.  \n\n1. ![Image of cow]  \n   **a. mother**  \n2. ![Image of dog]  \n   **b. cap**  \n3. ![Image of a doctor]  \n   **c. doctor**  \n4. ![Image of cap]  \n   **d. dog**  \n5. [Blurred Face]  \n   **e. cow**  \n6. ![Image of a bat]  \n   **f. bat**  \n7. ![Image of hills]  \n   **g. hills**  \n8. ![Image of a pencil]  \n   **h. rabbit**  \n9. ![Image of a plane]  \n   **i. forest**  \n10. ![Image of mountains]  \n   **j. plane**  \n\n---\n\n### **KNOW**  \n\n#### COMMON NOUNS  \n\nThe words **lion**, **lamb**, **rabbit**, **horse**, **dolphin**, **eagle**, **panda** are names of animals. The words **tail**, **ears**, **coat**, **mane**, **beak** are parts of the body of an animal. **Plain** is a name given to a flat open land.  \nAll these are names of things. These words are called **common nouns**.\n\n---\n\n[Page 4]\n**B. Complete the sentence using the correct word from the box.**\n\n**peak | joyously | neigh | chew**\n\n1. She climbed the mountain _________.  \n2. You should _________ your food well.  \n3. He _________ welcomed his friend.  \n4. I heard the _________ of a horse.  \n\n---\n\n**Fun With Grammar**  \n\n**KNOW**  \n**NOUNS**  \n\nRead these sentences.  \n\n- **Simba**, the lion is big and very strong.  \n- It has a **tail** that is very long.  \n- **Bimbi**, the lamb is small, soft and sweet.  \n- **Bunny**, the rabbit has **ears** as soft as **silk**.  \n- It has a **coat** as white as **milk**.  \n- **Dale**, the horse is handsome with a shiny **mane**.  \n- It gallops swiftly on the open **plains**.\n\n---\n\n[Page 5]\n**Word Magic**  \n**STUDY**  \n\nThis is a book called Dictionary.  \nIt has words, with letters arranged in an alphabetical order, from A to Z. To look for a word in a dictionary, we should know which letter of the alphabet it begins with.  \n\n**A** Write the first letter of these pictures in the given box.\n\n---\n\n[Page 6]\n**READ DEEPER**  \n**B. Answer the following questions in one word.**  \n1. Who is very strong?  \n2. Who is soft and sweet?  \n3. What is the name of the dolphin?  \n4. What sound does Bunny make?  \n5. How does the eagle catch its prey?  \n6. Who makes a neighing sound?  \n7. What sounds does Lee make?  \n\n---\n\n**THINK OUT LOUD**  \n**C. Express your views.**  \n1. What is the difference between Simba and Bimbi?  \n2. Who do you think is a wild animal; Bunny or Lee?  \n3. Which animal or bird would you like to be? Why?  \n4. Name all the sound words made by the animals and birds in the poem.\n\n---\n\n[Page 7]\nLearner’s Den  \n\n**RECOLLECT**  \n\n**A. Fill in the blanks with the correct words.**  \n\n1. Simba is ____________________ in size.  \n2. Bimbi makes a ____________________ sound.  \n3. Luna ____________________ in the cool waters.  \n4. The name of the eagle is ____________________.  \n5. The name of the rabbit is ____________________.  \n6. Dale has a shiny ____________________.  \n7. Lee chews on bamboo ____________________.  \n8. Bunny has ears that are as soft as ____________________.\n\n---\n\n[Page 8]\nRay, the eagle soars high up to the mountain peak,  \nWith its prey in the talons freeing its beak.  \nIt screeches over the sunny bay.  \nI feel like Ray today!  \n\nDale, the horse is handsome with a shiny mane,  \nIt gallops swiftly on the open plains.  \nIt can neigh in a loud way.  \nI feel like Dale today!  \n\nLee, the panda loves climbing a tree,  \nIt chews on bamboo shoots in glee.  \nIt huffs and puffs all day.  \nI feel like Lee today!\n\n---\n\n[Page 9]\nSimba, the lion is big and very strong.  \nIt has a tail that is very long!  \nIt can **roar** in a great way.  \nI feel like Simba today!  \n\nBimbi, the lamb is small, soft and sweet.  \nIt has a tail that is short and neat.  \nIt can **bleat** in a quiet way.  \nI feel like Bimbi today!  \n\nLuna, the dolphin, **leaps** joyously in the sea,  \nIt swims in the cool waters, wild and free!  \nIt whistles, clicks and **squeaks** away.  \nI feel like Luna today!  \n\nBunny, the rabbit has ears as soft as silk,  \nIt has a coat as white as milk.  \nIt can **cluck** in a happy way.  \nI feel like Bunny today!\n\n---\n\n[Page 10]\n1. THE ANIMAL SONG\n\n**Before We Begin**  \n1. Identify the animals/birds given below and colour their pictures.  \n(Images of animals are shown with blank spaces for their names)\n\n2. Which of these cannot live in your homes or farms?  \n_______________________________________  \n_______________________________________  \n\n3. What do you call those animals that are not dangerous?  \n_______________________________________  \n_______________________________________  \n\n4. Name two wild animals.  \n_______________________________________  \n_______________________________________  \n\n   Name two domestic animals.  \n_______________________________________  \n_______________________________________","sourceDescription":"","pageCount":10,"createdAt":"2026-03-16T16:16:32.117Z"},{"id":1,"userId":3,"board":"CBSE","className":"Grade 1","subject":"EVS","chapter":"Happy family","topic":"","extractedText":"[Page 1]\n**4. Happy Family**  \n\n**Get Set, Go!**  \nWrite an acrostic poem for family. For example, \"F - Fun, A - Always together, M - Mom's hugs,\" and so on.  \n\n**F** - Fantastic  \n**A** - Adorable  \n**M** - Mom's hugs  \n**I** - Incredible  \n**L** - Loving  \n**Y** - Young  \n\n(Page 52)\n\n---\n\n[Page 2]\n**FAMILY**  \nHello, I’m Manu!  \nMeet my family members, daddy, mommy, and my sister. We also have a pet dog.  \n\nWe love and take care of each other.  \nWe also share and help one another.  \nWe do a lot of things together.  \n\nBoth daddy and mommy go to office.  \n\nI also have grandparents, an uncle, an aunt, and cousins. They all live far away.  \nWe visit each other often.  \n\n---\n\n**A family is a group of people who live together and are related to one another.**  \n\n---\n\n**Members of the Family**  \nThere are many members in a family. Let us read about them.  \n\n- Your mother and father are your parents.  \n- Your mother’s mother is your grandmother.  \n- Your mother’s or father’s father is your grandfather.  \n- Your brothers and sisters are your siblings.  \n- Your uncle’s and aunt’s children are your cousins.  \n- Your cousins are your parents’ nieces and nephews.\n\n---\n\n[Page 3]\n**Checkpoint 1**  \nDescribe each family member. One is done for you.  \n\n- **Grandfather**: He is your father’s or mother’s father.  \n- **Grandmother**: She is your father’s or mother’s mother.  \n- **Uncle**: My father's or mother’s brother.  \n- **Aunt**: My father’s or mother’s sister.  \n- **Cousins**: Children of my uncles and aunts.  \n\n---\n\n**Activity**  \nAsk an elder to help you make your family tree. Paste pictures of your family members. You can add extra squares, if needed. You can make a special place on the tree for your pet too.\n\n---\n\n[Page 4]\n**Activity 2**  \nColour the given picture of a family.  \n\n---\n\n**Checkpoint 2**  \nChoose the correct words:  \nA. My mother’s father is my **grandfather/uncle.**  \nB. My mother’s sister is my **grandmother/aunt.**  \nC. My brother or sister is my **sibling/cousin.**  \nD. My uncle’s wife is my **cousin/aunt.**  \nE. My mother’s mother is my **grandmother/aunt.**  \n\n---\n\n**Types of Families**  \nA new family moved into Manu’s **neighbourhood.**  \nHe wondered if there were any friends he could play with. He was excited to see two boys getting out of the car.  \n\n---\n\n**Activity 3**  \nEach member in a family performs a different role. Watch a video on it. Understand how members of a family work together to be happy.\n\n---\n\n[Page 5]\n---\n\n**Hello! I am Manu. I live next door. Welcome to my neighbourhood. If you need anything, please let us know.**  \n**Hello! I am Vivek and he is my elder brother.**\n\n---\n\n**Vivek took Manu to meet his family. Manu was surprised. It was a very large family.**  \n\nBesides Vivek's parents, he also met his grandparents, uncle, aunt, and cousin.\n\nManu told his parents about the new neighbours and their big family. His mother explained, \"There are many types of families.\"  \n\n---\n\n**Nuclear family**  \nThis is a small family with one father, one mother, and their one or more children.  \nYour parents and siblings are your immediate family.  \n\n**Joint family**  \nThis is a large family that includes parents and their children, grandparents, uncles, aunts, and cousins, who live together in one house.  \nYour uncles, aunts, and cousins are your extended family.  \n\n---\n\n**Neighbours**  \nNeighbours are people who live near you. You might not know all your neighbours, but it is important to be kind and respectful to them. Neighbours help you when in need and celebrate happy occasions with you.  \n\n---\n\n**Activity 4**  \nIdentify the nuclear and joint families in the pictures.  \n*Image references marked: \"Nuclear family\" and \"Joint family.\"*\n\n---\n\n---\n\n[Page 6]\n**Interacting with Neighbours**  \n\nVivek the new neighbour came to play with Manuj.  \n\n“What a well-behaved child,” thought Manuj’s mother. He had greeted them all very politely.  \nWhen she gave them snacks to eat, he thanked her politely again.  \n\nBefore leaving, Vivek helped Manuj clean up his room.  \nThey picked up the games and toys in their proper places.  \n\nMother was happy to meet Vivek. She was happy that he was as “well-behaved child” like Manuj.  \n\n---\n\n**The following are some good habits that Manuj follows:**  \n- He greets everyone politely.  \n- He asks for permission before going out of the house.  \n- He never speaks in a loud voice and is never rude.  \n- He never interrupts when anyone is talking.  \n- He always uses words like, “Please”, “Thank you”, and “Excuse me”.  \n- He always knocks on the door before entering.  \n- He never touches other people’s belongings without their permission.  \n- He helps everyone in the family.  \n\n---\n\n**Activity**  \nFill in the details of any two neighbours:  \n| **Name** | **Nuclear or joint family** | **Language they speak** | **Festivals they celebrate** |  \n|---------|--------------------------------|--------------------------|----------------------------|\n\n---\n\n[Page 7]\n**Activity**  \n\nThis poem tells you about how you should behave with your neighbors.  \nRecite with your classmates.  \n\n**A GOOD NEIGHBOR**  \nWhen in doubt, they are always there.  \nListen to them, they always care.  \nShake hands and give a smile,  \nShare with them for a while.  \nThe neighborhood will be a happy retreat.  \n\n---\n\n**B. Tick (✔) the things that you must do and put a cross (✘) the things that you must not do while interacting with others.**  \n1. Greet everyone you meet. ✔  \n2. Go out to play without asking an elder. ✘  \n3. Complain about the snack that is packed for you. ✘  \n4. Wait for your turn to speak. ✔  \n5. Yell and throw tantrums if you need something. ✘  \n6. Speak in a soft and polite voice. ✔  \n7. Thank everyone for their birthday wishes and presents on your birthday. ✔  \n8. Ask for permission before using your sister's belongings. ✔  \n9. Disturb someone who is busy with their work. ✘  \n10. Say sorry for disturbing grandma's afternoon nap. ✔  \n\n---\n\n**A. Fill in the blanks.**  \n1. Your mother and father are your **parents**.  \n2. Your mother's or father's sisters are your **aunts**.  \n3. Everyone **cares** (cares/does not care) for each other in the family.  \n4. Your grandfather is your father's **father**.  \n5. Parents are your **immediate** family.  \n\n**Milestone**  \n\n---\n\n**B. Write two ways in which you help your family members.**  \n- **Grandparents**  \n  * Helping them in cooking.  \n  * Speaking to them and spending time with them.  \n- **Parents**  \n  * Helping with cooking.  \n  * Helping with cleaning the house.  \n- **Siblings/Cousins**  \n  * Helping with studies.  \n  * Helping them with their activities.\n\n---\n\n[Page 8]\n**C. Read about Patrick's family and answer the questions that follow.**\n\nPatrick lives in a city. His father, Mr. Montes, is an engineer and his mother, Mrs. Montes, is a teacher. He has a younger sister, Rosy. His family also consists of his grandfather and grandmother. He shares his room with his grandfather.  \nUncle John is his neighbour and his son, Peter, is his friend.  \n\n**Fill in the blanks with how Patrick is related to different members of the family.**  \n\n1. Patrick is Mrs. Montes’ **son**.  \n2. Patrick is Rosy’s **brother**.  \n3. Patrick is Aunt Lisa’s **nephew**.  \n4. Patrick is Grandfather’s **grandson**.  \n5. Patrick is Uncle John’s **nephew**.  \n\n---\n\n**D. Locate the different family members in the crossword.**  \n\n**Clues to solve the crossword:**  \n\n**Down**  \n1. She is my father’s mother.  \n2. Call him “Daddy.”  \n3. He also calls my father “Daddy.”  \n4. She is Mommy’s sister.  \n5. He is my uncle’s son.  \n\n**Across**  \n1. He is Mommy’s father.  \n2. He is Daddy’s brother.  \n3. She gave me birth.  \n4. She also calls my mother “Mommy.”  \n5. I do not recognize him.\n\n---\n\n[Page 9]\nE. Identify which neighbour’s act you will appreciate and why?  \n\n**Neighbour A:** Uncle John and Aunt Martha stay in Manuj’s neighbourhood. They have come to his home with a box of sweets. Their daughter has won a prize in a chess competition. They wanted to share their happiness with them.  \n\n**Neighbour B:** Mr. Goje’s house helper throws garbage all around instead of the dustbin. The neighbours have warned him many times, but he never listens.  \n\n**HOME CONNECT**  \nComplete the L1 and L2 worksheets given on Argus.  \n\n**STEP AHEAD**  \n**A.** Jaspreet went to her friend Ria’s house for a birthday party. There she met Ria’s family: her parents and her younger sister, Megan. Ria also introduced Mr. Cadbury, their cook, and Mr. D’Costa, their driver as her family members. Why do you think Ria introduced them as her family members?  \n\n**B.** Make a family photo album. Watch the video on Argus to learn how to create it. Take a picture and upload it.  \n\n**68**","sourceDescription":"","pageCount":9,"createdAt":"2026-03-16T16:04:16.043Z"}]
